[gd_scene load_steps=10 format=3]

; The Cistern Warden's fixture. Owned by tools/directors/boss_cistern.gd.
;
; Underscore-prefixed like _gate_test.tscn and _lookdev.tscn -- it is a harness,
; not a room the game ships. `Dungeon` will place a BossArena and a BossDoor in
; the deepest generated room at M4; this is the same two props in a hand-built
; chamber so the FIGHT can be proved before the floor exists to hold it.
;
; The shape is the one docs/GDD.md §5.1 describes and nothing more:
;
;   Chamber     26 x 26 m, ceiling 10. `BossDb`'s arena radius for the Warden is
;               11.0, so the seal ring comes up two metres inside the masonry --
;               far enough that the fence reads as its own thing rather than as
;               the wall, and the Warden's 6.2 m slam still has floor to spare
;               on every side of it.
;   Corridor    the way IN, south. The hero starts out here on purpose: the
;               arena seals behind him and the director has to photograph the
;               before as well as the after.
;   BossDoor    the far wall, north, where the stair would otherwise be. GDD
;               §5.1 -- the way down is behind the boss, and the longest walk on
;               the floor ends at the thing holding it.
;
; No pillars, and that is data rather than laziness: `BossDb` sets the Warden's
; `arena.cover` to false because a pillar here would teach the player to solve
; beat two by standing behind something, and beat two's answer is to walk INTO
; it. `BossArena._build_cover` reads the row; floors 2 and 4 get their posts for
; free from the same loop.

